    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q2",
      "question": "<p>The speed of a small jet aircraft was measured every 5 seconds, starting from the time it turned onto a runway, until the time when it left the ground.</p><p>The results are given in the table below with the time in seconds and the speed in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span>.</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td>Time (s)</td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>10</td><td>15</td><td>20</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>Speed (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span>)</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>10</td><td>18</td><td>28</td><td>42</td></tr></table><p>Using all of this information,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>estimate the length of runway used by the jet to take off. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the jet accelerated smoothly in these 25 seconds,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>explain whether your answer to part (a) is an underestimate or an overestimate of the length of runway used by the jet to take off. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
