      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:80mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: the curve y = sqrt(x) from O, with vertical lines at x = 4 and x = 9; a thin shaded rectangle of height y and width delta x under the curve at the point P(x, y).\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt x\"></span></p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(x, y)\"></span> lies on the curve.</p><p>The rectangle, shown shaded on Figure 3, has height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> and width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\delta x\"></span>.</p><p>Calculate</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{\\delta x\\to 0}\\sum_{x=4}^{9}\\sqrt x\\,\\delta x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
