      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q6",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:60mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q06-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4: sketch of y = g(x): a parabola arc decreasing to a minimum just right of the y-axis at x = 2, then a straight line increasing.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm g(x)\"></span>, where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)=\\begin{cases}(x-2)^2+1 &amp; x\\leqslant 2\\\\ 4x-7 &amp; x&gt;2\\end{cases}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{gg}(0)\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find all values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(x)&gt;28\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h\"></span> is defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h(x)=(x-2)^2+1\\qquad x\\leqslant 2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Explain why <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h\"></span> has an inverse but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g\"></span> does not. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Solve the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm h^{-1}(x)=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
