    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q7",
      "question": "<p>A small factory makes bars of soap.</p><p>On any day, the total cost to the factory, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds y\"></span>, of making <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> bars of soap is modelled to be the sum of two separate elements:</p><ul><li>a fixed cost</li><li>a cost that is proportional to the number of bars of soap that are made that day</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Write down a general equation linking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>, for this model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>The bars of soap are sold for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 2\"></span> each.</p><p>On a day when 800 bars of soap are made and sold, the factory makes a profit of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 500\"></span></p><p>On a day when 300 bars of soap are made and sold, the factory makes a loss of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pounds 80\"></span></p><p>Using the above information,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0.84x+428\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>With reference to the model, interpret the significance of the value 0.84 in the equation. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Assuming that each bar of soap is sold on the day it is made,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>find the least number of bars of soap that must be made on any given day for the factory to make a profit that day. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
