    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q9",
      "question": "<p>A research engineer is testing the effectiveness of the braking system of a car when it is driven in wet conditions.</p><p>The engineer measures and records the braking distance, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> metres, when the brakes are applied from a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\\,\\mathrm{km\\,h^{-1}}\"></span>.</p><p>Graphs of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> against <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}d\"></span> against <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}V\"></span> were plotted.</p><p>The results are shown below together with a data point from each graph.</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:42mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q09-figure-1.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5: graph of d against V, a curve from O increasing ever more steeply, through the marked point (30, 20).\"></figure><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:42mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q09-figure-2.svg\" alt=\"Figure 6: graph of log10 d against log10 V, a straight line with positive gradient crossing the vertical axis at the marked point (0, -1.77).\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Explain how Figure 6 would lead the engineer to believe that the braking distance should be modelled by the formula<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=kV^n\\qquad\\text{where }k\\text{ and }n\\text{ are constants}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\approx 0.017\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Using the information given in Figure 5, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=0.017\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find a complete equation for the model giving the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Sean is driving this car at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60\\,\\mathrm{km\\,h^{-1}}\"></span> in wet conditions when he notices a large puddle in the road <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> ahead. It takes him 0.8 seconds to react before applying the brakes.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Use your formula to find out if Sean will be able to stop before reaching the puddle. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
