    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q11",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:50mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-2019-june/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 8: sketch of the curve C, y = x^x for x &gt; 0, starting on the y-axis at a positive value, dipping to a minimum and then rising steeply.\"></figure><p>Figure 8 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^x\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find, by firstly taking logarithms, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of the turning point of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.<br>(<em>Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.</em>) <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(\\alpha, 2)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.5&lt;\\alpha&lt;1.6\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>A possible iteration formula that could be used in an attempt to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=2x_n^{\\,1-x_n}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Using this formula with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1.5\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4\"></span> to 3 decimal places, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>describe the long-term behaviour of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_n\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
